Description:

JMAP for Calendars now always serves JSCalendar 2.0.  A request using the
urn:ietf:params:jmap:calendars capability will be expected to work with
JSCalendar 2.0.

The event payloads that aren't tied to a request are JSCalendar 2.0 too: the
event and eventPatch of a CalendarEventNotification, and the jsevent and patch
of an iMIP notification sent to the imipnotifier.

CalDAV no longer supports the application/event+json media type.  It was never
standardized, and JSCalendar belongs to JMAP; a client that wants JSCalendar
should use JMAP for Calendars.  A GET asking for it in Accept now gets a 406,
and a PUT sending it now gets a 400.  application/calendar+json (jCal, RFC
7265) and application/calendar+xml (xCal, RFC 6321) are unaffected.


